<title>INDIA: Indian soybean steady, oil, meal down.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean steady, oil, meal down.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices remained steady in central Indian markets and plant delivery condition in very limited trading on Tuesday, dealers said.</p>
<p>Arrivals was around 2,500 rupees tonnes in central Indian markets. The Indore market will be closed on Wednesday as traders have called a strike to oppose new taxes.</p>
<p>Soyoil solvent was down by 100 rupees and soyoil refined was down 200 rupees per tonne on increased selling by plants and refineries. Volumes were dull and the undertone was easy.</p>
<p>Soymeal prices were slightly down as export demand was dull. Soymeal yellow was quoted at 281 rupees per tonne in export.</p>
<p>Rapeseed extraction was $112-113 per tonne for ready shipment and was $110 for March shipment in export. Rapeseed extraction was 3,850 rupees per tonne for ready delivery and was 3,800 rupees per tonne for March delivery in FOR condition.</p>
